ph F, the density of copies of F in Gn tends to a limit, then there is a natural \"limit object,\" namely a symmetric measurable function W:[0,1]2→[0,1]. This limit object determines all the limits of subgraph densities. Conversely, every such function arises as a limit object. We also characterize graph parameters that are obtained as limits of subgraph densities by the \"reflection positivity\" property. Along the way we introduce a rather general model of random graphs, which seems to be interesting on its own right."},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"lp-adamek-rosicky","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:39:10Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"J Ad\\'amek and J Rosick\\'y","title":"Locally presentable and accessible categories","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","year":"1994","optkey":"","optvolume":"","optnumber":"","optseries":"","optaddress":"","optedition":"","optmonth":"","optnote":"","optannote":""},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"maclane","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:39:10Z","response_hash":"27b0eeb020acac9e","fields":{"author":"Mac~Lane, Saunders","title":"Categories for the Working Mathematician","publisher":"Springer","year":"1998","optkey":"","optvolume":"","optnumber":"","optseries":"","optaddress":"","optedition":"","optmonth":"","optnote":"","optannote":""},"diffs":[{"field":"year","in_document":"1998","in_source":"1978","severity":"medium"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"markerModelTheoryIntroduction2002","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:39:10Z","response_hash":"f8937b197fdd4b30","fields":{"title":"Model {{Theory}} : {{An Introduction}}","shorttitle":"Model {{Theory}}","author":"Marker, David","year":"2002","month":"aug","publisher":"{Springer Science \\& Business Media}